{
  /* The desktop package cannot use the root tsconfig, which is why the root EXCLUDES it — and why
     nothing here was typechecked at all until an unbound identifier shipped through `bun run
     typecheck` unnoticed.

     The cause is that electrobun's SDK ships raw TypeScript (Electrobun 2 projects `.ts` sources,
     not `.d.ts`, under `.hutch/devkit/api` — see `extends` below), so importing it pulls its
     sources into the program as first-class files. `skipLibCheck` does not apply to those — it only
     suppresses `.d.ts` — and under the root's two strictest flags they emit 165 errors we cannot fix
     in a dependency. Dropping exactly those two flags brings electrobun to zero and leaves only our
     own code, which is the point of the exercise:

       exactOptionalPropertyTypes  → 160 of them, every `tooltip?: string` given `string | undefined`
       noUncheckedIndexedAccess    → the rest, plus one TS7030 in electrobun's Socket.ts

     Everything else stays on `strict`. That still catches unbound identifiers, wrong RPC shapes, and
     bad handler signatures — the failures this package actually has. Prefer narrowing this file back
     toward the root config over widening it. */

  "compilerOptions": {
    "allowImportingTsExtensions": true,
    "lib": ["ESNext", "DOM"],
    "module": "ESNext",
    "moduleResolution": "bundler",
    "noEmit": true,
    "noFallthroughCasesInSwitch": true,
    "noImplicitOverride": true,

    /* Where `electrobun/*` resolves from. Electrobun 2 ships no SDK on npm — `electrobun
       prepare` copies the release's SDK trees into a generated `.hutch/devkit` sysroot (run
       `bun run --cwd packages/desktop sync`, or any build, which syncs implicitly). Hutch also
       writes `.hutch/devkit/tsconfig.json` with the full 46-entry path map, and the intended
       wiring is to `extends` it — but that file sets `baseUrl`, which TypeScript 7 removed, so
       extending it fails the whole project with TS5102. These three entries are the entire
       `electrobun` surface this package imports; add one here if a fourth is ever needed, and
       revisit the `extends` when Hutch stops emitting `baseUrl`. */
    "paths": {
      "electrobun": ["./.hutch/devkit/api/sdks/main/index.ts"],
      "electrobun/main": ["./.hutch/devkit/api/sdks/main/index.ts"],
      "electrobun/view": ["./.hutch/devkit/api/browser/index.ts"]
    },

    "resolveJsonModule": true,
    "skipLibCheck": true,
    "strict": true,
    "target": "ESNext",
    "types": ["bun-types"]
  },
  "include": ["src/**/*", "tests/**/*", "scripts/**/*", "../../types.d.ts"]
}
